zark-gnome-app (1.2.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Translations: Spanish and wave 2 (pt_BR, pt, fr, it, ca, gl, de, nl)
    for the window, the desktop entry, the metainfo and the polkit
    policy (merged at build as xml:lang copies); commands and zark's
    output stay English, and so do Prepare's three lines on which disk
    zark takes, under a translated caption.
  * Prepare a New Drive says that the disk must be empty and that zark
    refuses one with partitions or a format it recognizes; the polkit
    texts of prepare and health follow.
  * A catalogue that cannot be loaded leaves the app in English.
  * Build-Depends: gettext. Tests against zark 2.3.2's reader.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:56:08 +0100

zark-gnome-app (1.1.3-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * A dialog when a backup's drive goes away (zark 2.3.1's drive_gone):
    the drive, the time it went and zark's hint, once per run and drive;
    quiet while zark's GNOME Shell extension 1.3 or later is active.
  * Build: lintian's binary-nmu-debian-revision-in-source suppressed for
    the PPA's per-series revision.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:58:30 +0100

zark-gnome-app (1.1.2-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fixes from the second eli checklist: Suspend from GNOME's menu is held
    during the app's run (a logind block inhibitor); a mount's result
    offers Open in Files and Unmount; the Prepare picker leaves out the
    disks the system uses; the attention icon in red for a run cut short;
    a closing line under zark's output at every end; dataset names keep
    their end in Exclude.
  * From the third: zark's percentage and time left, the peak hold gone;
    bytes only once a run's estimate grows with another round (zark 2.3.0
    after a resume); no foreign-version banner with a release candidate of
    zark installed.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:38:00 +0100

zark-gnome-app (1.1.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fixes from the first eli checklist: the launcher keeps python3 -I in
    the package; a redraw keeps the page's scroll and open months; the
    run's percentage comes from bytes only and is complete once the data
    is sent; backup points in local time; a drive mounted for browsing
    offers Open and Unmount and no Back Up.

